SUMMARY:The Great Gatsby
LOCATION:Broadway Theatre, 1681 Broadway, New York NY 10019
DESCRIPTION:<p>The party's roaring on Broadway! <em>The Great Gatsby</em>
  is a &ldquo;great, big Broadway extravaganza that explodes with life and
  energy&rdquo; (<em>Entertainment Weekly</em>). <br /><br />Directed by
  Marc Bruni (<em>Beautiful: The Carole King Musical</em>), this story of
  extravagance and longing features choreography by Dominique Kelley (<em>So
  You Think You Can Dance</em>), a book by Kait Kerrigan (<em>The Mad
  Ones</em>) and a jazz- and pop-influenced original score by Jason Howland
  (<em>Little Women</em>) and Nathan Tysen (<em>Paradise Square</em>).</p>
END:VEVENT
